# The bots' heatmaps: where the fights are on a map, learned from the
# matches players uploaded. A bot glances at where enemies usually show up
# and leans its roaming toward where the fights are. See doc/heatmaps.md.
#
# Note that these are inputs we check in rather than outputs of this build.
# They come out of the recording-heatmap tool that IW4x's client package
# carries, and whoever regenerates them commits the result here, the same
# way a changed menu or image is committed under zone_raw/.
#
./: heatmap{*}

# Installed beside IW4x's other loose files, in main/iw4x/x64, which is
# where the client looks for them once it has found none of its own in the
# player's storage directory.
#
# A fastfile would be the more usual home for game data shipped here, but
# the client reads a heatmap directly from disk on the server thread as a
# map loads and never through the engine's asset database. A zone would
# only add a step between the file and its single reader.
#
heatmap{*}: install = root/main/iw4x/x64/heatmaps/
